OL,3,GNEWSAHosepipe ban to continue
OL,4,Athroughout autumn
OL,5,
OL,6,FA hosepipe ban affecting more than 10
OL,7,Fmillion customers will remain in place
OL,8,Fthroughout autumn.
OL,10,FThe ban was first introduced by Thames
OL,11,FWater on 23 July, but the firm said its
OL,12,Freservoirs remained "far below" what
OL,13,Fwas normally expected in October.
OL,15,FIt said that although recent showers
OL,16,Fhad "brought a more autumnal feel",
OL,17,Fthey had not reversed the region's
OL,18,Frecord-breaking summer and ensuing
OL,19,Fdrought.
OL,23,APub: 17-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,325,320,200,140,0,100
